Recursion is a powerful programming technique that allows a function to call itself, indirectly enabling the function to split its task into smaller, more simple tasks. This concept is quite fundamental in programming, especially in languages like C, but it can sometimes be somewhat confusing.

This guide will provide a basic understanding of recursion, how it works, and how to implement it in C programming language.
<!--more-->

### Understanding Recursion

A function in programming is called recursive if it calls itself as a subroutine. Recursion is a common technique for solving problems which can be broken down into simpler, similar--------------------            if (Old_arrListContainsX)
            {
                PexAssert.AreEqual(Old_arrListLastIndexOfX, New_Ret);
