Here are some of those assertions, but they are quite complex.  The first one is checking the contract conditions post-modification to ensure the arraylist's Count is the same in both states, the other three are checking that the results of the methods IndexOf(), Contains(), and LastIndexOf() are consistent with each other and with the state of the ArrayList object before the method was called.
If you look at the last assertion, it is basically checking that the result of the IndexOf() method does not vary more than one position relative to the index returned by the LastIndexOf() method. This validates that the last occurrence of x in the ArrayList (or lack thereof) was accounted for correctly by the IndexOf() and LastIndexOf() methods.
